OsmoSync
Copyright (c) 2026 Scott Sharples. Licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

OsmoSync is written from scratch in Swift. Its protocol handling follows message layouts,
command numbers and connection steps documented or implemented by the projects below.
Source comments name the project each layout comes from.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OpenPocketCine
https://github.com/erik-sutton95/OpenPocketCine
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
You may obtain a copy of the License at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Used for: DUML frame layout and Wi-Fi datalink steps (DumlTransport), station join
(StationJoin, MulticamCommands), the 0x02/0x80 camera status layout, and gimbal, zoom
and tracking command numbers captured from DJI Mimo.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OsmoOffload
https://github.com/intermittech/OsmoOffload
Copyright (c) intermittech. Licensed under the MIT License.

Used for: the media list record layout, the delete-files command, the camera's file
download route, and the resume-into-a-.part-file download approach.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Osmosis
https://github.com/KonradIT/osmosis
Copyright (c) KonradIT. Licensed under the MIT License.

Used for: DUML captures that the layouts above were first worked out from.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DJI Osmo GPS Controller Demo
https://github.com/dji-sdk/Osmo-GPS-Controller-Demo

Used for: DJI's published R-SDK Bluetooth remote protocol (docs/protocol.md). No code
from that repository is included.

